---
summary: Risk-adjusted swing trading on liquid US large/mid-caps (scored on sortino)
# Optional: tickers this brief wants LOOKED AT. A search prior — they join the session's
# research focus set (the prompt's market digest, the holdout candidate pool, the episodic
# driver's session-start fetch), never the trading roster and never a gate. The roster is
# the other ticker surface, `config: universe:` far below; the two are different things.
# symbols:
#   - SMR
#   - CCJ
config:
  promotion:
    metric: sortino # sharpe | sortino | total_return — how every candidate is scored
  # # ── The rest of the surface, commented out ────────────────────────────────────────
  # # A mandate configures the whole RUN — which model thinks, what it may spend, how big
  # # its prompt gets, which names it starts from, what "good" is scored as. Every line
  # # below is one YAML line behind a "# ": bind it by removing exactly that prefix. The
  # # values are illustrative, not defaults; leave out the knobs this personality has no
  # # opinion about — an unset key simply keeps config.yaml's.
  # #
  # # A key that appears nowhere in this block is REFUSED, and a refusal is fatal at
  # # startup with the reason printed: the arena stays config.yaml's (safety mode, fill
  # # costs, promotion thresholds, the fit-set/symbol-holdout geometry, the output paths,
  # # the secrets). Two keys are CLAMPED to the disciplined direction only, marked below.
  # # Full reference: docs/configuration.md; the tables live in noctis/config/overlay.py.
  # research:
  #   # ── model seam: which brain runs the session, and where it is reached ──
  #   model: ollama_chat/noctis-qwen3:14b # LiteLLM provider/model for the driver
  #   base_url: http://localhost:11434/v1 # OpenAI-compatible endpoint (vLLM, Ollama, a proxy)
  #   # ── search shape: what the session is pointed at ──
  #   focus_size: 10 # cap on symbols enumerated into each prompt (a prompt-size lever)
  #   tuning_dispersion_penalty: 0.25 # λ × cross-symbol dispersion, in TUNING only
  #   draft_ttl_hours: 48 # sweep undecided __tmp/ drafts older than this into archive/
  #   memory_distill_every: 3 # distill MEMORY.md every N completed sessions (0 = off)
  #   # ── spend ceilings: how much one session may burn ──
  #   cost_profile: balanced # full | balanced | economy
  #   # ── CLAMPED, raise only: demand MORE evidence per verdict, never less ──
  #   min_trials: 20 # distinct journaled param sets before a verdict tool answers
  #   agent:
  #     model: anthropic/claude-sonnet-5 # driver fallback when research.model is unset
  #     loop: episodic # conversation | episodic | auto (auto flips at context_window ≤ 32768)
  #     thinking: "off" # the driver's reasoning dial — a watch-session switch
  #     coder_model: anthropic/claude-sonnet-5 # the dedicated authoring model
  #     coder_thinking: "on" # the coder's own reasoning dial
  #     coder_temperature: 0.2 # the coder's sampling temperature — sent only where the
  #     coder_seed: 7 # provider supports it (the local/OpenAI-compatible seam; Anthropic
  #     # # has neither parameter, so both are a clean no-op there). Neither buys
  #     # # determinism: they narrow a sampler, nothing more.
  #     coder_fallback_model: anthropic/claude-opus-4-8 # paid escalation for a spent coder
  #     coder_fallback_thinking: "off" # the escalated coder's reasoning dial
  #     max_escalations: 1 # escalations allowed per session (0 = never)
  #     max_iterations: 12 # tool-use rounds (conversation) / episodes (episodic)
  #     max_backtests: 30 # backtest calls + individual sweep trials
  #     sweep_trials: 24 # default Optuna trials for one run_sweep call
  #     max_author_calls: 9 # coder completions per session — the authoring bill
  #     max_tokens: 4096 # the driver's per-completion output ceiling
  #     coder_max_tokens: 16000 # the coder's output ceiling — the file's budget
  #     context_window: 32768 # whole-request budget (a small-context compat lever)
  #     episode_retries: 2 # corrective retries per episode when the model misfires
  #     coder_retries: 2 # private validator re-prompts per authoring job (each is a
  #     # # coder completion billed against max_author_calls)
  #     web_search: true # server-side grounding during FORMULATE/MATCH
  #     max_web_searches: 3 # and its per-session cap
  #     sweep_workers: 4 # parallel workers (results are identical whatever the count)
  #     worker_bar_budget: 3000000 # the memory guard that scales those workers down
  # data:
  #   history_days: 720 # lookback for the backfill of not-yet-ready symbols
  #   auto_backfill: true # whether that backfill runs at all
  #   # ── CLAMPED, lower only: spend LESS of the vendor budget, never more ──
  #   budget_usd: 40.0 # the cap the data cost preflight bounds every fetch against
  # observability:
  #   heartbeat_polls: 30 # -vv live-trading heartbeat cadence, in polls
  # qa:
  #   keep_last_runs: 5 # --debug QA run folders kept by prune-on-start
  # # ── the seed trading roster the research panel is drawn from — what is TRADED, not
  # # what is looked at (that is the symbols: list at the top). Upper-cased and
  # # de-duped the same way, and it must name at least
  # # research.fit_set_size + research.symbol_holdout_size symbols (8 as shipped) —
  # # fewer is fatal, because the symbol-holdout gate would go inert instead of being
  # # cleared, and neither of those two sizes is a knob a mandate may move.
  # universe: [AAPL, XOM, UNH, JPM, NVDA, WMT, CAT, GOOGL, SPY, IWM]
  # research_time_budget_minutes: 60 # wall-clock cap on one research session
  # time_limit_hours: 8 # wall-clock cap on ONE process — how long tonight lasts
  # run_limit_hours: 100 # compute cap on the whole RUN, across every stop/resume:
  # # once its cumulative runtime crosses this the run is `completed` (terminal, so it
  # # refuses resume). Frozen at creation — it is what makes two runs comparable on
  # # equal compute.
---

I want a believable, risk-adjusted record on liquid US large- and mid-cap names — deep
order books, tight spreads, no violent gaps — so backtested fills and the paper record
can be trusted. Hold for a day to a few weeks; avoid strategies that need many intraday
round-trips, because costs and fill realism dominate at that frequency.

Prefer effects with an economic reason to persist: trend continuation after a confirmed
break, pullbacks within an established trend, mean-reversion after overextension on
stable names, post-event drift. Shorting is allowed but optional — take it only when the
downside thesis is as well-formed as a long one, never by default.

Score on Sortino: upside volatility is welcome; downside deviation is what to minimise.
Cut losers on genuine breakdowns rather than hoping. A modest edge that survives
out-of-sample beats a spectacular one that doesn't. Avoid thin, headline-driven, or
recently-listed tickers.
